{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/326288-changelings-gentry-and-supernal-verges","id":326288,"title":"Changelings, Gentry, and Supernal Verges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-30T14:10:01-08:00","id":326288,"title":"Changelings, Gentry, and Supernal Verges","content":"During the talk about Supernal creatures in the Awakening 2E blog, I again thought about the new existence of Supernal Verges (areas in the Mortal world that are rewritten by the Supernal Realms). I wondered what would happen if a Exiled Gentry somehow stumbles into a Supernal Verge of Arcadia, and mistaking it for its own, colonizes the area for the Gentry. This leads to the questions of : 1. Can the Gentry use these Verges to reach Supernal Arcadia? and 2. How would Awakenings be affected if the Gentry conquer Supernal Arcadia?<br /> <br /> Then I focused on the Lost. How would a Changeling perceive a Verge of Supernal Arcadia, or any other Supernal Verge in this case? If curious, would a Changeling create a Contract with the Supernal via a Verge? COULD they? And if so, then how will this affect the mein of the Changeling in question? Its magic? How will this affect Changeling Society? Personally, I see the possibilities of another Court system that revolves around the five Supernal Realms. (An Antagonist idea?)<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T16:21:38-08:00","id":326391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/326288-changelings-gentry-and-supernal-verges#post326288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the talk about Supernal creatures in the Awakening 2E blog, I again thought about the new existence of Supernal Verges (areas in the Mortal world that are rewritten by the Supernal Realms). I wondered what would happen if a Exiled Gentry somehow stumbles into a Supernal Verge of Arcadia, and mistaking it for its own, colonizes the area for the Gentry. This leads to the questions of : 1. Can the Gentry use these Verges to reach Supernal Arcadia? and 2. How would Awakenings be affected if the Gentry conquer Supernal Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer this, first we must decide what is Supernal Arcadia. If we go with the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/falling-down/\" target=\"_blank\">Fallen World spoiler</a> that what we got on to hat is Supernal Realms:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages can. They call them \u201cThe Supernal World,\u201d and the concrete universe around them \u201cFallen.\u201d They exist in a liminal state, aware that the World of Darkness is a corrupted image cast by the Supernal\u2019s near-infinite layers of magical symbolism and occult meaning, warped by the Abyss into a Lie. They only have to concentrate to see the Supernal World \u2013 every symbol relating to their Awakened Path revealed in the surroundings. If they concentrate their magical awareness even further, the world seems on the brink of turning into a Supernal Realm \u2013 Obrimos see the energy barely contained within everything, Acanthus see Time and the push/pull of Destiny \u2013 and even glimpse the inhabitants of the Supernal out of the corners of their eyes. Despite their Gnosis, however, mages are trapped in the Fallen Word. They can look at the Supernal, but not touch, and the mind-blowing vistas of Supernal glory some mages Awaken to remain frustratingly out of reach. They can see how the symbols of the Supernal inform the Fallen World, but they can\u2019t become those symbols themselves, and experience the universe as pure magic. Not without Ascending. </div> </div> </div>So, in reality, Supernal Realms are &quot;source code&quot; of reality, divided in to 5 broad strokes. The Arcadia one is just connected to Fate and Time. Everything in the Realm is Symbol, so the Gentry need to be one to. As they have in Changeling Arcadia ( that is probably &quot;Lower Depths&quot; one ) bodies, True Fae clearly are not symbols, at least now. In my private cosmology, Strangers <b>were</b> inhabitants of Supernal Arcadia, but were cast out by Exarchs, when they took over the Realm. From the existence in Lower Depths realm that is known as Faerie to changelings. they stopped being symbols. But they still try to become, by invading the dreams of mortals - more people remember them and &quot;believe in them&quot;, more Gentry will become symbols and could enter Supernal Arcadia.<br /> <br /> As to your questions:<br /> 1. No, they cannot use Verges to reach Supernal Arcadia because they are not symbols - for now. Maybe if one of them become &quot;symbol-ish&quot; enough, but most of the time they just go to the &quot;Other&quot; Arcadia's garden, not proper palace, so to speak.<br /> <br /> 2. If Gentry would conquered Arcadia, they could overthrow the Exarch ruling it, maybe even Oracles. Souls of Awakened before gone to the Realm, only with going by the Astral Space, not Watchtowers - in the times of mythical Atlantis. So probably Awakenings still would be happen - but to the Realm of everlasting fight between symbols of human tyranny (Exarchs and Oracles) and inhuman horrors (Gantry). Eh, good times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then I focused on the Lost. How would a Changeling perceive a Verge of Supernal Arcadia, or any other Supernal Verge in this case? If curious, would a Changeling create a Contract with the Supernal via a Verge? COULD they? And if so, then how will this affect the mein of the Changeling in question? Its magic? How will this affect Changeling Society? Personally, I see the possibilities of another Court system that revolves around the five Supernal Realms. (An Antagonist idea?) </div> </div> </div><b>Awakening</b>'s cosmology posit Verges in Emanation Realms. As we do not have proper spoiler on those, I will use <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> for support here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Emanations</b><br /> Countless Emanation Realms surround the Supernal. These planes channel diluted primal arcane energies across<br /> the Abyss. Although they lie on the other side of the Abyss they are not the Supernal Realms themselves, so mages may travel them without risking soul loss. Most of them possess other hazards, however, from torrents of elemental \ufb01re to legions of rapacious spirits, so caution is still necessary. If a mage is willing to dare these hazards, the Emanations also provide an alternate route across the Abyss, and into associated realms via natural Irises. </div> </div> </div>Basically, Emanation Realms are subdomains, leading to proper Supernal Relm. Becuase in <b>Mage</b> 2ed Supernal Realms are &quot;source code&quot;, Emanation Realms would be any &quot;material&quot; form of Supernal could take - and in reality, working like Lower Depths Arcadia of <b>Changeling</b>. They would not be the same place, per se, but thwy would look very much like one another, had fantastical beasts inhabit them, and were govern by the rules of Fate and Time - on <b>Changeling</b> called by Wyrd. You would not need new Contracts, as they would mostly work the same as with normal Hedge and Arcadia. There is theory that Hegde is Emanation Realm of some alien part of Supernal Arcadia ( i.e. Faerie ).<br /> <br /> Interesting would be if in Verges would be Thorns. By many equated with Abyss variant of the Realm, in Verge they should not existence as there should not be any Abyss inside.<br /> <br /> As to how would this affect the Lost society - not so much. It's very weird topic for those changelings that work with Awakened enough to know they cosmology and magic to &quot;compare the notes&quot;. Of course Autumn Court could have something on this subject, but even they would not have solved it problem easily. It would be for PCs to explore the topic extensively. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-30-2014, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T21:59:21-08:00","id":327709,"title":"","content":"And yet a part of me is thinking that a Changeling might misinterpret it as that a part of Arcadia bypassed the Thorns and transformed the Mortal world, being that both Arcadias would be seen as similar. It's kind of like stumbling into one of Elizabeth's Tears in Bioshock Infinite. And also a part of me also thinks that a new Contract might be made because even though the Arcadias are similar, there have been talk that Changeling's Arcadia and Mage's Arcadia are two different zones. In that case, the magic may get influenced by the Verge in such a way, that the Changeling is transformed even further into a form that may mimic Arcadian magic, but may in some reality be superior to the home of the Gentry. That's why I want to have it as a sidebar for Changeling 2E. Supernal Verges may be influential if allowed in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}